   "text": "I read this as a thalidomide-type (4-substituted phthalimide\u2013glutarimide) group joined through an alkyne and a short PEG chain to a carbamate on a statin core.\n\n- **Left end:** a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group on the nitrogen of a phthalimide. The phthalimide carries a C\u2261C substituent at the 4-position of the benzene ring.\n- **Linker:** the alkyne continues as \u2013C\u2261C\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013O\u2013, ending in a carbamate.\n- **Right end:** the carbamate oxygen sits on C1 of the hexahydronaphthalene ring of a lovastatin/monacolin J-type core. The ring has methyls at C3 and C7 and a C=C\u2013C=C diene pattern. It carries the CH2CH2 chain to a 4-hydroxy-6-oxotetrahydropyran-2-yl lactone, which is drawn with wedges and hashes.\n\nFor the stereochemistry I used the natural lovastatin configuration. I took the lovastatin SMILES from memory and replaced its 2-methylbutanoyl ester with this carbamate linker, checking that the neighbour order at the C1 stereocentre stays the same. I did not independently re-derive each stereocentre from the wedges in the drawing. The glutarimide stereocentre is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: O=C(NCCOCCOCC#Cc1cccc2c1C(=O)N(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)O[C@H]1C[C@@H](C=C2[C@H]1[C@H]([C@H](C=C2)C)CC[C@@H]3C[C@H](CC(=O)O3)O)C"
